      "text": "To solve the given equation $7^{x+7} = 8^x$, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Rewrite the equation using properties of exponents:**\n   \\[\n   7^{x+7} = 8^x\n   \\]\n   This can be rewritten as:\n   \\[\n   7^x \\cdot 7^7 = 8^x\n   \\]\n\n2. **Use the property of exponents:** If $a^m = a^n$, then $m = n$.\n   Thus, \n   \\[\n   7^x = 8^x\n   \\]\n\n3. **Divide both sides by $7^x$:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{7^x}{7^x} = \\frac{8^x}{7^x}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   1 = \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)^x\n   \\]\n\n4. **Express the equation in logarithmic form:** Since $\\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)^x = 1$, we can use the property of logarithms that $\\log(a^b) = b \\log(a)$.\n   \\[\n   x \\log\\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right) = 0\n   \\]\n\n5. **Solve for \\( x \\):**\n   Since $\\log\\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right) \\neq 0$, we use:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{1}{\\log\\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Given that \\( x = \\log_b 7^7 \\), we express \\( \\log_b 7^7 \\) in terms of the above solution:**\n   \\[\n   \\log_b 7^7 = x\n   \\]\n   Using the property of logarithms:\n   \\[\n   \\log_b 7^7 = \\frac{7x}{7}\n   \\]\n\n7. **Substitute the value of \\( x \\) obtained earlier:**\n   \\[\n   \\log_b 7^7 = \\frac{7}{\\log\\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)}\n   \\]\n\n8. **Finally, set \\( \\log_b 7^7 \\) equal to \\(\\frac{1}{\\log\\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)}\\) to conclude that:**\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{7}{\\log\\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( b \\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).",
